  "judge_notes": [
    "Merged all von Frey applications (CFA, partial sciatic nerve ligation single dose, repeated dosing once/twice daily, antagonist pharmacology, harmine experiments) into ONE Von Frey assay per rubric — same apparatus, same outcome, only manipulations differ.",
    "Added a separate Home-cage body weight + food/water intake monitoring assay (only the gptoss candidate omitted it; the data are explicitly reported and described in methods as monitored throughout the 14-day protocol). Scored E1 as Home cage and E8 as Yes accordingly.",
    "Excluded Fos immunohistochemistry — it is a histological readout (not behavioural).",
    "Dosing schedule set to 'multiple' for both ayahuasca and harmine because the paper tested both acute and repeated (twice-daily 14-day) regimens of each compound.",
    "Housing handling and enrichment scored 'not_reported' (paper does not address); light cycle 'not_reported' since direction (light/dark phase of testing) not specified.",
    "B1 in Von Frey scored 0 (single threshold measure); B2 set to 'No' because measurements at multiple post-treatment hours are between-session timepoints rather than within-session temporal binning (one candidate over-scored).",
    "Tail flick assigned setup_restrain=yes (mice in restriction tubes during recording), unlike other free-movement assays."
